proposed_schema_format:
We propose a slimmed JSON Schema profile derived from draft-07 with the following constraints: 1) Support 'type', 'properties', 'required', 'additionalProperties' (boolean only), 'enum', 'minimum'/'maximum' for numbers, 'minLength'/'maxLength' for strings, and 'format' limited to 'uuid','email','date-time'. 2) Disallow 'oneOf'/'anyOf' for top-level parameter unions; allow lightweight 'oneOf' only inside strictly-named helper objects. 3) Authoring ergonomics: prefer explicit 'required' list; avoid deep nesting beyond 3 levels; include 'x-example' freeform property for downstream error messages. Example allowed schema snippet as string:
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "user_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "uuid",
      "x-example": "3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6"
    },
    "limit": {
      "type": "integer",
      "minimum": 1,
      "maximum": 100
    }
  },
  "required": ["user_id"],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
